# KEEPERS RED AND OWNED: a keeper here runs on every gate, its refusal said and not failed — and a
# pinned keeper that passes FAILS its row until its line goes (tools/gate.sh, keeper_row). Each line:
# the keeper, then who owns its red and why. A keeper is pinned only with an owner named.
trap-marks the cores/pool lane — pid_is_zombie calls strrchr (a call out), so every allocation reaches a trap unsaid
clock-holds the cores/pool lane — six blocking calls in avra_cores.c and avra_pool.c hold no clock
read-lists the ledger owner — seven queries past their read-list ceilings (law_findings, collect_members, …)
warm-edit the ledger owner — a warm edit's rule_nodes and rule_runs past their ceilings
cutoff-witness the ledger owner — one literal edited proves and checks past its bounds
defects the defects owner — collect_enum_zero_all and collect_enum_zero_nullable trap at run
inputs the lanes of the rows it names — six sites unclassified (avra_fn_declared, avra_ctx_*, avra_cores_*)
